    {
      "id": 29,
      "title": "Scope and limitations",
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 8,
        "y": 72,
        "w": 16,
        "h": 8
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "One shared managed instance for cache, synchronization and gateway rate limiting. All graphs show instance totals, **not separate dev/prod usage**.\n\nTimeweb supplies authenticated HTTPS database and host exporters; Valkey itself stays private. The monitoring credential only accesses metrics and is separate from database accounts.\n\nNo key values, key names, channel names or slowlog command arguments are collected. Network/application latency and per-user OOM/write failures are unavailable from these aggregate counters. Missing samples stay **No data**; an idle hit ratio is undefined. AOF/RDB persistence is not HA or a backup."
      }
    }
